      "title": "orrery",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## orrery · H3 reel (one screenplay, one clip per run)\n\n`SCENE` lines split the screenplay into clips; the `segment` widget counts up by itself, so **Roll** next N clips plays them and **Restart** goes back to clip 1. Keep the seed fixed (the node sets it).\n\n- **Orrery Continue** starts every clip after the first with the last 22 frames of the one before, picture and sound, under a noise mask (Masked AV, from [H3 Continuum](https://github.com/ukr8b3g-cmyk/ComfyUI-H3-Continuum), MIT). `length` already counts those frames.\n- **Orrery Film** trims them off again, keeps every clip's take under `output/h3_context/orrery_film/` and joins the reel so far into `film.mp4` there (its `film` output). Rendering a clip again replaces it and drops the ones that continue it; a `(test)` scene's take is kept but left out of the film.\n- The editor marks every SCENE with its clips and the time left; the timeline beside it shows the clips.\n\nThe **Orrery Prompt** node is the whole of orrery: write in its **Prompt** tab (this workflow opens with a quickstart; **New** has the other modes), roll it in **Test** without queueing, and rate what comes out in **Gallery**: the ratings steer the next rolls. **Roll** in the node queues this graph (next N clips or images: how many runs); what the Save node writes is logged to the gallery with the picks that made it.\n\n- `seed` drives the rolls and the sampler (Random Noise).\n- The model runs through the Orrery Prompt (`model` in, `model` out to the scheduler and the guider): its `LORA:` lines go on the model, and the results under the prompt show the live preview while it samples.\n\n[orrery on GitHub](https://github.com/pyros-projects/orrery) · [the prompt language](https://github.com/pyros-projects/orrery/blob/main/docs/dsl.md) · [H3 screenplays](https://github.com/pyros-projects/orrery/blob/main/docs/h3.md)"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## orrery · H3 reel (one screenplay, one clip per run)\n\n`SCENE` lines split the screenplay into clips; the `segment` widget counts up by itself, so **Roll** next N clips plays them and **Restart** goes back to clip 1. Keep the seed fixed (the node sets it).\n\n- **Orrery Continue** starts every clip after the first with the last 22 frames of the one before, picture and sound, under a noise mask (Masked AV, from [H3 Continuum](https://github.com/ukr8b3g-cmyk/ComfyUI-H3-Continuum), MIT). `length` already counts those frames.\n- **Orrery Film** trims them off again, keeps every clip's take under `output/h3_context/orrery_film/` and joins the reel so far into `film.mp4` there (its `film` output). Rendering a clip again replaces it and drops the ones that continue it; a `(test)` scene's take is kept but left out of the film.\n- The editor marks every SCENE with its clips and the time left; the timeline beside it shows the clips.\n\nThe **Orrery Prompt** node is the whole of orrery: write in its **Prompt** tab (this workflow opens with a quickstart; **New** has the other modes), roll it in **Test** without queueing, and rate what comes out in **Gallery**: the ratings steer the next rolls. **Roll** in the node queues this graph (next N clips or images: how many runs); what the Save node writes is logged to the gallery with the picks that made it.\n\n- `seed` drives the rolls and the sampler (Random Noise).\n- `LORA:` lines come out on `lora_stack`, for a loader with a `lora_stack` input (LoraManager, Efficiency …), which is not part of this core-nodes workflow.\n\n[orrery on GitHub](https://github.com/pyros-projects/orrery) · [the prompt language](https://github.com/pyros-projects/orrery/blob/main/docs/dsl.md) · [H3 screenplays](https://github.com/pyros-projects/orrery/blob/main/docs/h3.md)"
